<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Icherisheher</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Walled City of Baku, Old City of Baku, Inner City of Baku</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Icherisheher is the historic walled old city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baku">Baku</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a>, on the shore of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caspian-sea">Caspian Sea</a>. Its streets contain the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maiden-tower">Maiden Tower</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palace-of-the-shirvanshahs">Palace of the Shirvanshahs</a>, mosques, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caravanserai">caravanserais</a> and bathhouses, enclosed by medieval walls. The Walled City of Baku, with the Maiden Tower and the palace, was declared a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a> in 2000.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/icherisheher.jpg" alt="Icherisheher" width="320" height="453" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sefer azeri · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%C4%B0%C3%A7%C9%99ri%C5%9F%C9%99h%C9%99r_kollaj%C4%B1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
